      "premise": "There was once a lineage of 'Ear Cleaners' who recorded the final moments of non-human beings as sound. One winter night, the dying words of a yokai are entrusted to the static of an old radio. Guided by a mysterious voice drifting from the dawn airwaves, a young recorder begins to trace the lingering passions of forgotten apparitions and the memories of their time being loved by humans. It is a story of the final testaments—resembling prayers—left behind by those fading into nothingness."
